538	/// Tauri command: forget an identity's local material WITHOUT any network step.
539	///
540	/// The escape hatch for an identity that can no longer be removed through the normal flow
541	/// because its PDS account no longer exists — deleted from another device, purged
542	/// server-side, or migrated away. In every such case the deletion endpoints can only answer
543	/// with an opaque 401: the PDS deliberately does not expose account existence, so an unknown
544	/// DID and a wrong password are indistinguishable (see
545	/// `crates/pds/src/routes/delete_account.rs`). The request/confirm flow can therefore never
546	/// make progress, and without this the identity would be stranded in the wallet forever.
547	///
548	/// This wipes the DID's Keychain material and clears any pending-removal marker. It
549	/// deliberately does NOT tombstone the did:plc: the DID may already be retired, or (the
550	/// migrate-away case) the device key is no longer a rotation key and the identity now lives
551	/// on another PDS — so "forget locally" only promises to remove the identity from THIS
552	/// device. The frontend states that plainly and gates the call behind the biometric prompt.
553	///
554	/// Returns `was_last_identity` (mirroring `RemovalOutcome`) so the UI can route back to
555	/// onboarding rather than the identity list when the wallet is now empty.
556	#[tauri::command]
557	pub fn forget_identity_locally(did: String) -> Result<bool, RemovalError> {
558	    wipe_local(&IdentityStore, &did)?;
559	    clear_removal_pending_best_effort(&did);
560	    no_identities_remain()
561	}
